    ('GCUKIP/25-26/002', '2026-04-14', '- Will get his final degree certificate by October 2027 he said he will then start his one year internship\n- This will be an internship which is on the same level as an indian internship but it will not be NMC approved \n- He said that he will finish this by the end of 2028 \n- I told him that the GMC or AMC may or may not recognize this later on because this is going to be 3 years from now \n- Told him to do the internship anyway. If we can use it later on, we will \n- If we can\'t then he\'ll have to do fy1', 'ralph_goocampus1'),
    ('GCUKIP/2023/082', '2026-04-14', 'The doctor is currently coordinating a conference call to discuss progress regarding medical internship requirements and registration with EPIC. There are discussions surrounding the AMC route for credentialing, as it may offer a more efficient path compared to the traditional competency pathway. The involvement of Dr. Prachi and the creation of necessary documentation appear to be central to moving forward.\n\n\n\nCONFERENCE CALL DETAILS\n\nParticipants: Jason, Dr. Prachi, and the daughter.\nScheduled Time: Between 1:00 PM and 2:00 PM.\n\n\nINTERNSHIP REQUIREMENTS\n\nInquiry: Conducting a review of the medical internship documents required by Dr. Prachi.\nStatus: Documentation needs will be verified during the conference call.', 'jeswin_goocampus1'),
    ('GCUKIP/2023/082', '2026-04-14', 'Executive Summary: \n\nThe current situation indicates no significant operational issues or roadblocks. The doctor is maintaining open communication and adjusting priorities as needed, ensuring support for personal matters while keeping professional responsibilities steady.\n\n\n\nCOMMUNICATION STATUS  \n\nThe doctor is engaging in regular communication with patients and colleagues.  \nNo concerns were expressed about ongoing operations.\n\n\nPERSONAL STATUS  \n\nThe doctor acknowledged a focus on personal matters, particularly regarding family.  \nThe situation is being managed without affecting professional obligations.', 'jeswin_goocampus1'),
    ('GCUKIP/2023/082', '2026-04-14', 'Dr. Pachi is preparing to engage with the EPIC system for her professional registration. Initial steps involve scheduling a session with Dr. Balan, an experienced doctor in Australia, at a cost of 5,500. Additional services such as CV editing will incur extra fees, with overall costs contingent on her service selections. The situation is complicated by geopolitical factors affecting the job market, which previously impacted another candidate’s opportunities. Planning and coordination are required to secure consultations and tailor services for Dr. Pachi’s career pathway effectively.\n\n\n\nINITIAL CONSULTATION COSTS  \n\nSession with Dr. Balan: 5,500  \nCV editing services provided by third parties: charges will apply, specifics to be determined based on package selections.  \n\n\nEPIC REGISTRATION EXPENSES  \n\nExpected cost for EPIC registration: 50 GBP (subject to actual charges).  \nAdditional service fees will be determined based on the chosen package model; one-time payment options are available.  \n\n\nSERVICE PACKAGE OPTIONS  \n\nTwo models for pricing:  \nAll-inclusive package for one-time payment covering EPIC and service charges.  \nSeparate payments for EPIC fees and additional consulting service charges.  \n\n\nFUTURE COORDINATION  \n\nNeed to confirm Dr. Balan’s availability for the consultation slots which may be limited.  \nFollow-up discussion scheduled for tomorrow to finalize service options and costs.  \n\n\nJOB MARKET CONSIDERATIONS  \n\nGeopolitical factors have introduced uncertainties in the job market which affect Dr. Pachi’s chances of securing postgraduate opportunities.  \nPrevious candidates highlight the need for careful consideration in future planning and adjustments for application pathways.', 'jeswin_goocampus1'),
    ('GCUKIP/2022/078', '2026-04-14', 'The doctor is currently addressing a communication from the GMC regarding an outdated letter. A draft response has been sent for review and edits. The doctor is experiencing some uncertainty but is actively working to rectify the situation. Timely action is required to ensure compliance and avoid further delays.\n\n\n\nCOMMUNICATION DETAILS  \n\nThe doctor received an email from the GMC regarding an outdated letter.\nA draft reply has been prepared and sent for review.\n\n\nRESPONSE STATUS  \n\nThe doctor is required to review and edit the draft.\nNo specific deadline was mentioned for the response.\n\n\nFOLLOW-UP ACTIONS  \n\nThe doctor plans to check the draft response soon.\nFurther communication is needed to clarify GMC\'s requirements.', 'jeswin_goocampus1'),
    ('GCUKIP/24-25/003', '2026-04-14', 'The doctor is currently available for a brief consultation of 10 to 20 minutes. An urgent meeting has been scheduled, indicating the need for immediate attention. However, specific concerns regarding the meeting details are not yet clear.\n\n\n\nAVAILABILITY\n\nThe doctor is free for a consultation.\nThe duration of the available time is between 10 to 20 minutes.\n\n\nMEETING URGENCY\n\nAn urgent meeting has been mentioned.\nConfirmation regarding the exact nature and details of the meeting is pending.\n\n\nPOTENTIAL ROADBLOCKS\n\nThe lack of clarity on the meeting details may hinder preparation for the consultation.\nTime constraints due to the meeting may limit discussion during the available consultation period.', 'jeswin_goocampus1'),
    ('GCUKIP/24-25/003', '2026-04-14', 'The doctor is currently navigating a challenging educational and career landscape. They are considering several courses, including the BMJ course for one-year access and one E-Integrity course, while showing interest in courses such as ATLS and CRISP. Although they are preparing for clinical attachments, the competitive nature of obtaining jobs in the UK, especially post-MRCP, remains a significant concern. The doctor faces uncertainty regarding job prospects due to the prioritization bill and escalating competition, hindering their ability to focus on training roles.\n\n\n\nCOURSES AND TRAINING:\n\nBMJ Course: One-year access recommended.\nE-Integrity Courses: One course to be completed; the second course is optional.\nATLS Course: Expressed interest.\nCRISP Course: Considering enrollment.\n\n\nMRCP EXAMINATION:\n\nNext MRCP Slot: Scheduled for January next year.\nPrevious Timing: Initially discussed for September but determined to be too tight for completion this year.\n\n\nCLINICAL ATTACHMENT:\n\nStatus: Doctor is preparing for a clinical attachment.\nExpected Communication: Details to be received via email by the end of this month.\n\n\nMARKET COMPETITION:\n\nIncreasing Difficulty: Competition for jobs is intensifying due to the prioritization bill.\nJob Acquisition Timeline: Doctors who pass the PLAB exam typically secure jobs after 3-4 years, requiring additional qualifications (MRCP or MRCS) for consultancy roles.\nRecent Scoring Trends: Previous borderline scores have become more common; higher scores now necessary for GP roles.\n\n\nONGOING CHALLENGES:\n\nLack of slots in IMT: Issues with allocation due to the prioritization bill.\nUncertainty in Job Focus: Consideration to shift towards non-training roles amid the current economic climate surrounding healthcare.', 'jeswin_goocampus1'),
    ('GCUKIP/24-25/018', '2026-04-13', '- She\'s currently in India \n- WIll stay here until she has to go back to the UK for her Clinical assessment \n- She was asking about the Ireland pathway \n- She is considering taking the FMGE too', 'ralph_goocampus1'),
    ('GCUKIP/2022/078', '2026-04-08', 'STATUS OF DOCUMENTS  \n\nThe doctor is currently waiting for one document from the college.  \nA verification report has been received from ECFMG and has been forwarded again.\n\n\nCOMMUNICATION DELAYS  \n\nThere has been a delay in corresponding with relevant parties regarding the IELTS matter, initially expected to take only one week.  \n\n\nEXPLANATION FOR DELAY  \n\nThe doctor plans to attach an email explaining a technical issue that prompted changes in scores, which will be sent out after drafting.', 'jeswin_goocampus1'),
    ('GCUKIP/2023/010', '2026-04-08', 'DOCTOR\'S COMMUNICATION STATUS\n\nDoctor has checked the email from Mr. Saviour.\nDoctor has not yet responded to the email.\n\n\nVISA DOCUMENTATION\n\nThe doctor will send a dummy accommodation letter for visa purposes.\n\n\nCLINICAL ATTACHMENT FEES\n\nAn administrative fee of around 200 pounds for documentation is required.\nOther trusts may charge fees up to 500 pounds, making the current fee reasonable.\nThe attachment itself is stated to be free of charge.', 'jeswin_goocampus1'),
    ('GCUKIP/24-25/030', '2026-04-08', 'PAYMENT STATUS\n\nThe second installment is overdue, originally due within 70 days after clearing the IELTS in March.\nThe outstanding second installment is 472,000.\nThe final installment is 500,000 plus 90,000 GST.\n  \n\nPREPARATION TIMELINE\n\nFour to five months of preparation is recommended from India.\nNo need to hurry, but the doctor will require around 45 days in the UK, consisting of 12 days of classes and 30-35 days of practice.\n  \n\nCOST BREAKDOWN\n\nAdditional accommodation costs in the UK: Approximately 300-400 pounds (40,000-50,000).\nCourse costs are included in the package.\nFlight tickets (one way) expected to be between 25,000-50,000 INR.\nPLAB 2 fees are estimated at 130,000 INR.', 'jeswin_goocampus1'),
    ('GCUKIP/2021/082', '2026-04-08', 'DOCUMENTATION STATUS\n\nPrevious submissions include documentation for ECFMG and Ireland Medical Council.\nThe doctor has submitted a request for Epic and Notary Camp verification.\n\n\nPASSPORT ISSUE\n\nThe doctor\'s passport has changed and is now expired.\nCurrent systems do not allow for the upload of updated passport information.\n\n\nCOMMUNICATION STRATEGY\n\nThe doctor plans to email ECFMG to request updates using their Intel ID.\nContent of the email will include a request for passport update and any relevant account details.\n\n\nCOST IMPLICATIONS\n\nA verification fee of Rs.5000 has already been paid for the EPIC verification.\n\n\nNEXT STEPS\n\nFollow up email correspondence to ensure passport update is processed.\nClarification needed on the validity of the submitted report with the changed passport.', 'jeswin_goocampus1'),
